   "etymology": "Uncertain. Proposals include:\n* Inherited from Proto-Indo-European, akin to Ancient Greek σφάλλω (sphállō, “to overthrow”). This appears phonetically incompatible with the current reconstruction of the Greek term's ancestor as Proto-Indo-European *(s)gʷʰh₂el- (“to stumble”).\n* Borrowed from South Slavic, from Proto-Slavic *xvaliti (“to praise”), compare Macedonian фали (fali), Serbo-Croatian hváliti /хва́лити.",
